## Why This Is Asked
Tests automation of security incident response in a complex SAP on AWS environment, focusing on real-world tooling and cross-account controls.

## Key Concepts
- RFC anomaly detection via CloudWatch and GuardDuty
- Cross-account IAM roles with MFA-protected STS elevation
- Automated network isolation through security group modifications
- Secrets rotation for SAP credentials in AWS Secrets Manager
- Step Functions orchestration for workflow and audit trails

## Code Example
```javascript
{
  "Comment": "SAP incident response state machine",
  "StartAt": "DetectAnomaly",
  "States": {
    "DetectAnomaly": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [
        {
          "Variable": "$.alert_type",
          "StringEquals": "RFC_ANOMALY",
          "Next": "AssumeRemediationRole"
        }
      ],
      "Default": "LogAndDismiss"
    },
    "AssumeRemediationRole": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:assume-role-with-mfa",
      "Next": "IsolateHost"
    },
    "IsolateHost": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:isolate-sap-host",
      "Next": "RotateCredentials"
    },
    "RotateCredentials": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:rotate-sap-secrets",
      "Next": "NotifyAndLog"
    },
    "NotifyAndLog": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:notify-and-log",
      "End": true
    },
    "LogAndDismiss": {
      "Type": "Pass",
      "End": true
    }
  }
}
```

## Minimal IaC Sketch (Terraform)
```hcl
resource "aws_sfn_state_machine" "sap_incident_response" {
  name     = "sap-incident-response"
  role_arn = aws_iam_role.stepfunctions_role.arn
  definition = file("${path.module}/state_machine.json")
}

resource "aws_iam_role" "cross_account_remediation" {
  name = "sap-remediation-role"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow",
      Principal = { AWS = "arn:aws:iam::123456789:role/sap-incident-response-role" },
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
      Condition = { Bool = { "aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent" = true } }
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_security_group_rule" "sap_isolation" {
  count = 1
  type        = "ingress"
  from_port   = 0
  to_port     = 0
  protocol    = "-1"
  description = "Emergency isolation"
  source_security_group_id = aws_security_group.sap_management.id
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests the ability to respond to SAP-specific security incidents with cross-account trust, emergency privilege handling, and auditable containment across Prod, Shared, and DR environments.

## Key Concepts

- Automated incident response using Security Hub, Step Functions, and Lambda
- Emergency cross-account roles with MFA enforcement
- SAP HANA on EC2 access control with STS-based JIT (Just-In-Time) privilege elevation
- Key management via KMS with automated rotation strategies
- Network containment using security groups and PrivateLink with end-to-end auditability

## Code Example

```javascript
{
  "Comment": "SAP incident response workflow",
  "StartAt": "ValidateTrigger",
  "States": {
    "ValidateTrigger": {
      "Type": "Choice",
      "Choices": [{
        "Variable": "$.detail.findings[0].Severity",
        "StringEquals": "CRITICAL",
        "Next": "AssumeEmergencyRole"
      }]
    },
    "AssumeEmergencyRole": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:assume-emergency-role",
      "Next": "VerifyMFA"
    },
    "VerifyMFA": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:verify-mfa",
      "Next": "RevokeSessions"
    },
    "RevokeSessions": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:revoke-sap-sessions",
      "Next": "JITElevation"
    },
    "JITElevation": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:grant-sap-access",
      "Parameters": {
        "DurationSeconds": 3600,
        "PolicyArns": ["arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/SAPOperatorAccess"]
      },
      "Next": "RotateKeys"
    },
    "RotateKeys": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:rotate-kms-keys",
      "Next": "IsolateResources"
    },
    "IsolateResources": {
      "Type": "Task",
      "Resource": "arn:aws:lambda:...:function:isolate-sap-endpoints",
      "End": true
    }
  }
}
```

**IaC Snippet for Emergency Cross-Account Trust Role:**

```hcl
resource "aws_iam_role" "emergency_sap_role" {
  name = "SAP-Emergency-Response-Role"
  assume_role_policy = jsonencode({
    Version = "2012-10-17",
    Statement = [{
      Effect = "Allow",
      Principal = {
        AWS = "arn:aws:iam::PROD-ACCOUNT:root"
      },
      Action = "sts:AssumeRole",
      Condition = {
        Bool = { "aws:MultiFactorAuthPresent" = "true" }
      }
    }]
  })
}

resource "aws_vpc_endpoint_service" "sap_privatelink" {
  acceptance_required = true
  network_load_balancer_arns = [aws_lb.sap_nlb.arn]
  allowed_principals = [aws_iam_role.emergency_sap_role.arn]
}
```

**Critical Success Factors:**
- All actions must be logged to CloudTrail with immutable audit trails
- Emergency role assumptions require separate out-of-band approval for production access
- JIT elevation tokens must have strict TTLs (typically 1-4 hours) with automatic expiration
- Key rotation must maintain backward compatibility during transition periods?
